From 093592e3952ea28adc8cef033dc0ef63aa649777 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: reaper <theunbounddeveloper@outlook.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 18:39:21 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] ASUS DDNS: the client and its leftovers are deleted

ASUS DDNS (asuscomm.com) has been refused on this firmware since 2026-10-23, but its code stayed.
Deleted: rc/asus_ddns.c (registration, unregister, the token client and its firewall rules), the
watchdog's ASUS branches, httpd's unregister handler and Warden's ASUS server seed; inadyn's two
asuscomm plugins compile to nothing. The DDNS refusal and the Let's Encrypt seed stay. Also in
these files: watchdog.c keeps the Guest Portal's DNS forwarder running (the Guest Portal commit).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 release/src/router/inadyn/plugins/asuscomm.c  |   6 +
 .../src/router/inadyn/plugins/asuscommv2.c    |   6 +
 release/src/router/rc/asus_ddns.c             | 466 ------------------
 release/src/router/rc/rwarden.c               |  30 +-
 release/src/router/rc/watchdog.c              |  20 +-
 5 files changed, 28 insertions(+), 500 deletions(-)
 delete mode 100644 release/src/router/rc/asus_ddns.c

